; Mitten glove, posed to wrap a grip. Its origin sits at the CENTRE of the grip
; it holds, so the arm rig can drop it straight onto a weapon's grip marker
; regardless of which weapon that is.
;
; No fingers. A cartoon hand is a mitten with a thumb, and at the size these are
; drawn -- a hand's width from the camera in first person, a few pixels in third
; -- four separate fingers cost eight meshes to say something nobody can see.
; What does read is the silhouette: a fat rounded palm, a thumb across the top
; of the grip, and a cuff at the wrist.
